.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Coulson (1939) wrote the Huckel eigenvalues of a linear chain of n atoms in closed form, E_k=\alpha+2\beta\cos(k\pi/(n+1)), and Frost and Musulin (1953) turned the ring result E_k=\alpha+2\beta\cos(2\pi k/n) into a drawing: put a regular n-gon, one vertex pointing down, inside a circle of radius 2|\beta|; the heights of the vertices are the orbital energies. Both closed forms (~chemistrykit.quantum.systems.huckel.linear_polyene_eigenvalues, cyclic_polyene_eigenvalues) are checked here against numerical diagonalization.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/quantum/huckel/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_03_coulson_frost_closed_forms_thumb.png
